  "schema": "transfer-ordinary-index-read-endpoint-v1",
  "scope": "Concrete current-overlay index reads distinguish unavailable from absent data, with every present byte value treated as an existing identifier. Available existing-ID read derives exact semantic duplicate error; unavailable read refuses success without being counted as a duplicate control. Whole same-action Ordinary delivery with source-separated volume/height keys, decoded original parent height and existing parent ID entry is rejected for every extractor/body outcome and read availability. Executable body NV frame preserves that ID until inspection, and current height read preserves the original decoded height; parent and queue remain original after enclosing refusal. No successful body, desired index error, stable-height callback or rollback poststate is assumed. Initial state/conversion/decoder inputs and inherited proof/token/Rust/key/store/tree/native/block/durability remain interfaces. Full Transfer open; no native or semantic negative-control credit. Seven handwritten declarations qualified in the first guarded attempt. Read availability false cannot be counted as a semantic duplicate; the exact duplicate-error theorem explicitly derives it only when the actual modeled read is available and any value is present. Whole delivery refusal is unconditional on extraction/body outcomes and read availability, under explicit original-state height/decoder/ID and conversion observations. It does not assert raw error cache rollback or native Host fault reachability. No native, semantic control or durable-publication evidence.",
